  // p70 new units (owner 17 Nov 2026)
  "unit.type.halberdier":"Halberdier",
  "unit.type.royal_archer":"Royal Archer",
  "unit.type.crossbowman":"Crossbowman",
  "unit.type.light_cavalry":"Light Cavalry",
  "wiki.title.unit.halberdier":"Halberdier",
  "wiki.title.unit.royal_archer":"Royal Archer",
  "wiki.title.unit.crossbowman":"Crossbowman",
  "wiki.title.unit.light_cavalry":"Light Cavalry",
  "wiki.text.unit.halberdier.why":"The halberdier keeps the enemy at bay: his halberd strikes from 2 tiles and hits riders half again as hard.",
  "wiki.text.unit.halberdier.how":"He needs a halberd and armour from the Armory. The Swordsmith forges halberds – switch its production to Halberds in the building window.",
  "wiki.text.unit.halberdier.tips":"- Put halberdiers in the front rank; they reach past the man beside them.",
  "wiki.text.unit.royal_archer.why":"The royal archer shoots like an archer but lasts like a swordsman.",
  "wiki.text.unit.royal_archer.how":"He needs a bow and light armour from the Armory. He has more health and the Swordsman's defence.",
  "wiki.text.unit.royal_archer.tips":"- Dearer than an archer, but he does not fall at the first hit.",
  "wiki.text.unit.crossbowman.why":"The crossbowman shoots strong bolts up to 7.5 tiles. A bolt ignores half of the enemy's armour – the unit against knights.",
  "wiki.text.unit.crossbowman.how":"He needs a crossbow and light armour from the Armory. The Bowyer makes crossbows (switch production to Crossbows), the Tailor sews light armour from cloth.",
  "wiki.text.unit.crossbowman.tips":"- A crossbow needs iron as well as wood.",
  "wiki.text.unit.light_cavalry.why":"The light cavalryman is a fast mounted fighter with a sword.",
  "wiki.text.unit.light_cavalry.how":"He needs a sword and light armour from the Armory, and a tamed horse from the Stables. Mounted, he is half again as fast. After a ride of 5 tiles or more he opens the fight with a charge: one heavy blow (35 hit points before armour).",
  "wiki.text.unit.light_cavalry.tips":"- Without Stables you cannot train light cavalry.\n- Ride in, strike, ride away and come back: every new ride gives a new charge.\n- His own look comes later.",
  "wiki.text.unit.catapult.why":"The Catapult breaks enemy walls, Towers, Gates and buildings from afar – 100 hit points a Stone, from 3 to 18 tiles away.",
  "wiki.text.unit.catapult.how":"Order a Catapult in the Builder's Workshop: Builders build it beside the workshop (30 Wood, 6 Iron). Then train a Recruit in a Barracks as its crew; he walks to it and rolls it.",
  "wiki.text.unit.catapult.tips":"- Each throw uses a Stone; it holds 10. It loads them beside a store or from a Military Wagon near it.\n- It shoots only at buildings, slowly and from behind the soldiers.\n- Right-click an enemy building with the Catapult selected to send it there.",
  "wiki.text.unit.military_wagon.why":"The Military Wagon carries supplies for the army: Stones for the Catapults, food and Torches for the soldiers.",
  "wiki.text.unit.military_wagon.how":"Train a Recruit in a Barracks as its driver; he needs a free Horse Wagon with its horse. Beside a store the wagon loads 30 Stones, 20 food and 10 Torches.",
  "wiki.text.unit.military_wagon.tips":"- Catapults within 6 tiles get Stones from it.\n- Soldiers within 6 tiles eat from it and take their night Torches from it.\n- It does not fight; keep it behind the army.",
  "wiki.text.resource.halberd.why":"The halberd is the halberdier's weapon.",
  "wiki.text.resource.halberd.how":"The Swordsmith forges it from 4 Iron and 3 Wood when its production is set to Halberds; it is kept in an Armory.",
  "wiki.text.resource.halberd.tips":"- A halberd adds 120 % attack and a reach of 2 tiles.",
  "wiki.text.resource.crossbow.why":"The crossbow is the crossbowman's weapon.",
  "wiki.text.resource.crossbow.how":"The Bowyer makes it from 6 Wood and 1 Iron when its production is set to Crossbows; it is kept in an Armory.",
  "wiki.text.resource.crossbow.tips":"- A crossbow adds 90 % attack.",
  "wiki.text.resource.light_armor.why":"Light armour (a padded jacket) protects Swordsmen, Royal Archers, Crossbowmen and Light Cavalry.",
  "wiki.text.resource.light_armor.how":"The Tailor sews it from 3 Cloth; it is kept in an Armory.",
  "wiki.text.resource.light_armor.tips":"- Light armour adds 15 armour.",
